All `insert_item` `Err` errors are already converted to `String` upstream (every site that calls it in `memory/mod.rs` and `memory/store.rs` uses `.map_err(|e| e.to_string())?` before returning). This means `import_core`'s `Err(_) => report.skipped += 1` discards a fully-formed Chinese error message produced for exactly this purpose. Bind it:

```
Err(e) => {
    eprintln!("[mem_import] item skipped due to storage error: {e}");
    report.skipped += 1;
}
```

so future storage regressions leave a breadcrumb in logs instead of silently inflating `skipped`. (Do not regress to `Err(_) => report.skipped += 1` without logging.)

